---
const stats = [
  { count: 91.4, decimals: 1, suffix: '%', label: 'Historical win rate' },
  { count: 3.5, decimals: 1, prefix: '~', suffix: '%', label: 'Avg. targeted monthly return' },
  { count: 1.5, decimals: 1, suffix: ' yrs', label: 'Battle-tested in beta' },
  { count: 99.98, decimals: 2, suffix: '%', label: 'Execution engine uptime' },
];
---

<section class="section results" id="results">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The results</span>
      <h2>Numbers that <span class="text-accent">compound</span></h2>
      <p>Performance you can audit. Here's what the Vectora engine has delivered across our client base.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-grid">
      {stats.map((s, i) => (
        <div class="card stat reveal" style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 80}ms`}>
          <span
            class="stat-num"
            data-count={s.count}
            data-decimals={s.decimals}
            data-prefix={s.prefix ?? ''}
            data-suffix={s.suffix ?? ''}
          >{s.prefix ?? ''}0{s.suffix ?? ''}</span>
          <span class="stat-label">{s.label}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <figure class="quote reveal">
      <blockquote>
        “I spent years blowing up accounts on emotional trades. With Vectora the plan just <em>runs</em> — same rules, every session. My drawdowns are smaller and I finally sleep through the night.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">DR</span>
        <span><b>Daniel R.</b><small>Full-time futures trader · 2 years with Vectora</small></span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p class="disclaimer">
      Trading involves substantial risk of loss and is not suitable for every investor. Past performance is not indicative of future results. Figures shown are illustrative.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .stat-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; }
  .stat { text-align: center; padding: 2rem 1rem; }
  .stat-num {
    display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.7rem); line-height: 1.1;
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, #FFFFFF 25%, #5BE6AE 95%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent;
  }
  .stat-label { color: var(--c-text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; display: block; }

  .quote {
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) auto 0; max-width: 780px; text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    background: var(--grad-soft); border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg); backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
  }
  blockquote { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.45; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--c-text); }
  blockquote em { color: var(--c-accent-bright); font-style: normal; }
  figcaption { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; text-align: left; }
  .avatar { width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #062A1B; background: var(--grad-accent); }
  figcaption b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); color: var(--c-text); }
  figcaption small { color: var(--c-text-dim); }

  .disclaimer { text-align: center; color: var(--c-text-dim); font-size: 0.78rem; max-width: 660px; margin: 2.5rem auto 0; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) { .stat-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
</style>
